  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening local capacities and agriculture to improve rural livelihoods</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Jacmel has worked in Fonds Jean Noel since 2005 in supporting health services, and livestock activities.  The majority of this population are subsistence peasant farmers with an annual income of US$ 375 with some of them living in extreme poverty (less than a dollar a day).
These small producers belong to an organisation, &#x201c;l&#x2019;association des fraternit&#xe9;s de Fonds Jean No&#xeb;l&#x201d; made up of 14 peasants&#x2019; groups. Access to agricultural inputs and technical support is practically non-existent. In addition to that soil erosion and unsustainable farming practices have significantly decrease the productivity of land and the livelihoods of people living in this locality.
The community is poorly served, both by the government bodies and non governmental organisations. This situation has been compound by the fact that the community organisation and participation in decision making is weak. 
The project will strengthen farmers&#x2019; organisational structures and provide farmers with new agricultural tools, improved seeds, and other agricultural inputs, as beneficiaries have identified a huge need for agricultural activities and this will contribute to improving their lives and their livelihoods. They will be trained on modern agricultural techniques, on conservation and soil improvement and on management of farm income.</narrative>
  </description>
